    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d214-a4">

                <pb facs="0512" n="416" sameAs="frus:frus1879/pg416"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3 in Mr. Hathorne’s No.
                    42.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hathorne to Mr. Kirk.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Consulate</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Zanzibar</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1878-12-27"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 27,
                        1878</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your letter of this day’s date, wherein you
                    inform me that the negroes referred to (unlawfully taken from the American bark
                    Laconia to Her Britannic Majesty’s ship London by the officers of the latter
                    vessel) have been returned to their ship, is received, and in reply thereto
                    would state that I shall be glad to receive the report of the circumstances of
                    the case referred to.</p>
                <p>I wish to correct the date of my letter delivered you this morning, which was by
                    me erroneously written December 26, and should have been December 27.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>W. H. HATHORNE,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">United States
                            Consul.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
